   "topic_id": 2,
   "title": "Chunk Size and Chunking Strategies for RAG QA over Internal Documentation",
   "description": "This topic examines how chunking decisions shape retrieval-augmented question answering over a large internal engineering wiki. It centers on a hands-on sweep of fixed chunk sizes with token overlap, scored by answer correctness against a benchmark of human-written questions, and extends to three popular alternatives: semantic chunking via embedding breakpoints, sentence-window retrieval, and prepending page titles to chunks. Together they frame the trade-off between context sufficiency and retrieval precision, and where tuning effort is best spent.",
