   "topic_id": 1,
   "contributor": "0x90d828e09dfd698f0b0c575845c5771246f6544e",
   "title": "Schedules, Warmup, and Data Mixing in LoRA Fine-Tuning for Invoice Extraction",
   "description": "With the LoRA adapter for invoice JSON extraction held fixed, this study tests the training levers recipes often disagree on: cosine versus constant learning rates, warmup length, mixing general instruction data into batches, curriculum ordering of documents, and freezing the embedding layer. Small open models are scored on exact-match extraction F1 over real invoices plus a general instruction-following check to measure forgetting. Readers learn which choices matter, which are dead ends, and how to balance extraction accuracy against general ability.",
